descriptionByLocale.en:
You like risk analysis and customer relationship, you have a sense of negotiation and are ready for a new challenge!

Zurich France, a leading international group company, offers companies customized solutions and innovative insurance concepts for the transfer, financing and management of their risks. We are convinced that our development and success depend on those of our employees: Training, career development, international mobility are a reality for all of us.

Your role

Senior policyholder A&H alongside Head A&H Zurich France is responsible for:

-Participation in the implementation of the strategy for the development of the subscription line in France, in line with the Group's subscription strategy;

-The development of the A&H portfolio in France within Zurich France;

-The development and consolidation of the offer of services and relations with brokers and customers;

-The establishment of the necessary partnerships to best serve our clients, and to monitor and monitor these partnerships in line with local and Group requirements and regulations;

-Participation in the organisation of the line and interactions with the various internal departments (Management, Commercial, Claims Management etc.), and achievement of the priority objectives of profitability of the profit and loss account A&H.

Main activities

Participation in the establishment of a local strategy to develop our A&H portfolio in France in line with the Group's appetites and policies.

- Managing and developing its portfolio

-Follows the analysis, evaluation and negotiation of new contracts and renewals according to the scope (national and/or international) of the branch according to the underwriting authorities;

- Conducts risk studies and analyses;

-Decides the acceptance of the risk and assesses the conditions under which the Group can cover it, in accordance with guidelines and levels of authority;

-Proposes or validates the draft contract to intermediaries or customers and participates in the negotiation;

-Develops and negotiates a suitable contract proposal or contract amendment;

-Informs and updates control, reporting and subscription systems;

- Develop and strengthen relationships with brokers and clients to achieve development and retention goals

- Ensures the consistency and transparency of information transmitted to brokers and customers;

-Works in collaboration with commercial teams;

-Participates in negotiating meetings with brokers and clients;

-Organizes the prospecting of new customers, the development of cross selling and the saturation of customers already in portfolio.

- Ensure compliance with local and Group regulations

-Ensure proper compliance with rules and regulations;

-Participates in technical and legal watch.

- Participate in the interface with other business departments (Underwriting services, Sinisters, Finance, Matrix, etc.) to improve customer service and team efficiency

-Participates in information relays and cooperation between internal teams;

-Contributes to the sharing of good practices;

- Participate in the construction of products and services sold

-Participates in updating existing insurance policies and developing new policies;

-Contributes to the development of marketing tools

Qualifications

- Significant experience (5 years minimum) in Subscription in the relevant or similar branch(s);

-Oriented towards performance and results;

-In-depth knowledge of the products concerned;

- Controlling computer tools;

- Common English essential.

Knowledge

-Aware of responsibilities, reliability, exemplaryness, integrity;

-Initiative spirit and systematic proposal of solutions;

-Capacity to evolve in complex situations, high stress resistance;

- Team spirit, benevolence, external and internal relational ease;

-Spirit of synthesis and rigour;

-Sense of service, availability to intermediaries and clients as well as internal staff.

-Commercial fitness: excellent communication, ability to make public presentations

-Ability to assess and manage risks.

Remuneration: 70ke - 85ke according to remuneration + variable

The position is based in Paris 17th

You think you're made for this job?

Dare to join a new challenge, come join us! Apply quickly!

Zurich Insurance recognizes the diversity of our workforce as an asset. We recruit talented people from diverse backgrounds with unique perspectives. Taken together, diversity and inclusion bring us closer to our common goal: to exceed the expectations of our customers. Zurich has a policy of equal opportunities in employment. Our goal is to attract and retain the best professionals without discrimination based on disability, race, nationality, religion, sexual orientation, gender expression or age. Position open to persons with disabilities.

Zurich France attaches great importance to the protection of personal data. To learn more about the processing of your personal data as part of our recruitment operations, please consult our Information Notice available on the Zurich France website (www.zurich.fr - "Career") at the following address: https://www.zurich.fr/en/carriere

You have a right of access, rectification, deletion, limitation, opposition to the processing of your personal data, as well as a right to portability. For the exercise of your rights, you can contact our Data Protection Officer by email ( dpo.france@zurich.com ), or by mail: Zurich France, Data Protection Officer, Legal and Compliance Service, 112 avenue de Wagram, 75017 Paris.

Apply »

